Add a cheap ack-only `ping` handler so the client stale-watchdog can distinguish 'alive but quiet' from 'dead' before reconnecting (audit P3). Exclude it from the per-socket rate-limit buckets and do not log it:
```ts
  /** Client stale-watchdog liveness probe (frontend socketHealthService.probeSocket). Ack only. */
  @SubscribeMessage('ping')
  handlePing(): { ok: true; server_time: number } {
    return { ok: true, server_time: Date.now() };
  }
```
(Nest passes the returned value to the socket.io ack callback the client supplies via `socket.timeout(2500).emit('ping', cb)`.) Until this exists the client probe times out after 2.5 s and falls back to the old reconnect.
